\begin{corollary}[counterexample; the proposed global filling]\hypertarget{tag-030D}{}\label{push:src:B.4.1}\label{push:B41}
\StatementRecord{push:src:B.4.1}{proved}{030D}{\SeriesRef{push:src:B.4.33}, \SeriesRef{push:section:B.1}, \SeriesRef{push:section:B.2}, \SeriesRef{push:src:B.4.19}}

The actual punctured $S^6$ family has no proper
Hausdorff complex-analytic filling after any finite
cover of $w=0$. In particular, a proper flat filling
with smooth total space and reduced normal-crossings
centre does not exist. There is no positive least
semistable exponent, no equivariant analytic filling
to descend, and no central multiplicity data for
such a descent.
\end{corollary}


\begin{proof}
\begin{enumerate}[label={$\langle1\rangle$\arabic*.},leftmargin=*]
\item Theorem \ref{push:src:B.4.33} below proves the stronger assertion
allowing arbitrary singular central spaces and
multiplicities. A hypothetical filling after any
initial cover remains proper after a further cover;
the theorem excludes that further cover as well.
The local constructions in \ref{push:section:B.1} and \ref{push:section:B.2} and the
partial filling \ref{push:src:B.4.19} therefore cannot be completed
to the requested global object.
\end{enumerate}
\end{proof}

push:src:B.5.1:
\begin{corollary}[counterexample; the premise of a global central fibre]\hypertarget{tag-031A}{}\label{push:src:B.5.1}\label{push:B51}
\StatementRecord{push:src:B.5.1}{proved}{031A}{\SeriesRef{push:src:B.4.33}}

There is no central fibre or descent resolution
of the requested proper analytic filling of the
actual $S^6$ family. Its proposed integral homology,
fundamental group, central Euler number and
nearby-cycle comparison are therefore undefined.
\end{corollary}


\begin{proof}
\begin{enumerate}[label={$\langle1\rangle$\arabic*.},leftmargin=*]
\item Theorem \ref{push:src:B.4.33} excludes the underlying proper
analytic space after every finite parameter cover.
An invariant of that nonexistent central fibre
cannot be computed by assigning it the topology
of a local or auxiliary model. The local topologies
and necessary degeneration conditions proved above
retain exactly their stated hypotheses. Restriction of the actual punctured family to a parameter circle
gives its smooth mapping torus; that monodromy is computed in Part C.
\end{enumerate}
\end{proof}
